      model: "Comparison statement: revenue $150,000 and $180,000, change +$30,000 (+20.00%); gross profit $60,000 and $63,000, change +$3,000 (+5.00%); profit for the year $18,000 and $18,000, no change (0.00%). Gross profit margin: 2026 = 60,000 ÷ 150,000 × 100 = 40.00%; 2027 = 63,000 ÷ 180,000 × 100 = 35.00%. Profit margin: 2026 = 18,000 ÷ 150,000 × 100 = 12.00%; 2027 = 18,000 ÷ 180,000 × 100 = 10.00%. Comment: revenue rose by 20% but gross profit by only 5%, so the gross profit margin fell by 5 percentage points; prices were probably cut to sell more, or ingredient costs rose and were not passed on. Profit is unchanged in dollars, so the extra sales produced no extra profit. The owner should review prices or supplier costs, but higher prices could reduce customer numbers.",
