      model: "Gross profit margin: 2026 = 140,000 ÷ 400,000 × 100 = 35.00%; 2027 = 132,000 ÷ 440,000 × 100 = 30.00%. Profit margin: 2026 = 40,000 ÷ 400,000 × 100 = 10.00%; 2027 = 30,800 ÷ 440,000 × 100 = 7.00%. Current (working capital) ratio: 2026 = 90,000 ÷ 50,000 = 1.80:1; 2027 = 104,000 ÷ 65,000 = 1.60:1. Acid test (liquid) ratio: 2026 = 40,000 ÷ 50,000 = 0.80:1; 2027 = 36,000 ÷ 65,000 = 0.55:1. Profitability: revenue rose 10% but gross profit margin fell 5 points, so phones were sold at lower prices or bought at higher cost; profit fell by $9,200 despite higher sales. Liquidity: inventory rose from $50,000 to $68,000 while liquid assets fell from $40,000 to $36,000 and current liabilities rose, so cash is being tied up in unsold phones and the business relies on suppliers and the bank. Advice: stop cutting prices and clear older phone models to release cash; order in smaller quantities. Drawback: clearance prices lower the margin further in the short term, and smaller orders may lose supplier discounts.",
